ACC-006 — Engineering Evidence

Document ID: ACC-006
Title: Engineering Evidence
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines Engineering Evidence, the validated information upon which Engineering Understanding is constructed.

Engineering Evidence transforms Engineering Observations into trustworthy inputs for engineering cognition through validation, qualification, and contextual evaluation.

2. Scope

This specification applies to all information used to support engineering conclusions within the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework.

Engineering Evidence may originate from, but is not limited to:

Engineering observations
Measurements
Sensor data
Engineering drawings
BIM/CAD models
Engineering calculations
Simulations
Laboratory tests
Inspection reports
Photographs and videos
Standards and regulations
Engineering documentation
Expert assessments
3. Canonical Definition

Engineering Evidence is validated and contextually relevant information that supports, contradicts, or qualifies Engineering Understanding.

Engineering Evidence is not merely collected information.

It is information that has been evaluated for relevance, reliability, integrity, and applicability.

4. Characteristics

Engineering Evidence SHALL possess the following characteristics.

4.1 Observation-Derived

Engineering Evidence SHALL originate from one or more Engineering Observations.

4.2 Validated

Engineering Evidence SHALL undergo evaluation appropriate to its intended engineering use.

4.3 Relevant

Engineering Evidence SHALL be applicable to the engineering context in which it is used.

4.4 Traceable

Engineering Evidence SHALL maintain traceability to its originating observations and sources.

4.5 Explainable

Engineering Evidence SHALL support transparent engineering reasoning.

4.6 Contextual

Engineering Evidence SHALL be interpreted within its engineering context.

4.7 Evolvable

Engineering Evidence MAY be strengthened, weakened, superseded, or invalidated as new observations become available.

5. Relationships

Engineering Evidence occupies the central position in the Atlas cognitive pipeline.

Engineering Reality
        │
        ▼
Engineering Observation
        │
        ▼
Engineering Evidence
        │
        ▼
Engineering Understanding

Engineering Evidence:

Is derived from Engineering Observations.
Supports Engineering Understanding.
Is consumed by Engineering Reasoning.
May be preserved by Engineering Memory.
May contribute to Engineering Knowledge through repeated validation.
6. Responsibilities

Engineering Evidence is responsible for:

Supporting engineering understanding.
Justifying engineering reasoning.
Enabling explainable decision-making.
Maintaining traceability.
Recording supporting and contradicting information.
Preserving engineering confidence.
7. Normative Requirements

Engineering Evidence SHALL:

Be derived from Engineering Observations.
Maintain traceability to its source.
Preserve contextual information.
Support explainable engineering reasoning.
Be available for independent review.

Atlas SHALL NOT construct Engineering Understanding from information that has not been evaluated as Engineering Evidence.

8. Non-Goals

Engineering Evidence does not:

Represent Engineering Understanding.
Perform engineering reasoning.
Produce engineering decisions.
Replace engineering judgment.
Represent engineering memory.
Represent engineering knowledge.
9. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY define evidence quality models, confidence metrics, provenance models, and evidence classification mechanisms without changing the canonical definition established by this specification.